> My "Ralph Nader Nethack" is just the same as regular nethack,
> except that all objects are fully identified.

I don't see any point to writing a patch for this.  Regular nethack
already comes with a feature called "wizard mode" where you can identify
anything you have just by pressing Control-I.

See http://www.spod-central.org/~psmith/nh/wizmode.txt for more
information about wizard mode.

Similarly, if you want to save copies of your savefiles to restore your
game when you die, you can do this in regular nethack just by pressing
capital X to enter explore mode, and THEN saving your game.  Next time you
reload the game it will ask if you want to keep a copy of the savefile;
just say yes.


